# Same-origin IPFS. Browsers fired bursts of ~1 MB image requests at public
# gateways, which answered many with 429 text/plain; Chrome (ORB) and Safari
# (CORS) then refused to render them. Proxying through this origin removes the
# cross-origin failure, and each edge node caches the immutable bytes (Pinata
# sends an 11-month max-age). An edge function and a serverless function with
# a `durable` CDN policy were both tried for one cross-node copy; neither
# produced a durable cache layer, and the function adds an execution time
# limit, so the plain proxy stays. Must stay above the SPA fallback.
/ipfs/*  https://gateway.pinata.cloud/ipfs/:splat  200
/*    /index.html   200
